  "content": {
    "id": "p67-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Use trial and error to find as many integer zeroes of $P(x)$ as possible, then use long division to find the other factors.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p67-q18-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=2x^4-5x^3-5x^2+5x+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Integer zeroes: $-1,1,3$.\n$P(x)=(x-1)(x+1)(x-3)(2x+1)$; the remaining zero is $-\\frac{1}{2}$.",
          "worked": "Test the possible integer zeroes $\\pm1,\\pm3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=2-5-5+5+3=0\\\\P(-1)&=2+5-5-5+3=0\\\\P(3)&=162-135-45+15+3=0\\\\P(-3)&=162+135-45-15+3=240\\end{align*}$$\nThus the integer zeroes are $1,-1,3$.\nLong division by $x-1$ gives quotient $2x^3-3x^2-8x-3$ and remainder $0$. The successive subtraction results are\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)-2x^3(x-1)&=-3x^3-5x^2+5x+3\\\\{}-(-3x^2)(x-1)&=-8x^2+5x+3\\\\{}-(-8x)(x-1)&=-3x+3\\\\{}-(-3)(x-1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nLong division of the quotient by $x+1$ gives $2x^2-5x-3$ with remainder $0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x^3-3x^2-8x-3)-2x^2(x+1)&=-5x^2-8x-3\\\\{}-(-5x)(x+1)&=-3x-3\\\\{}-(-3)(x+1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nFactorise the quadratic:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(x+1)(2x^2-5x-3)\\\\&=(x-1)(x+1)(x-3)(2x+1).\\end{align*}$$\nThe remaining zero is $-\\frac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 130
      },
      {
        "id": "p67-q18-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=6x^4-25x^3+17x^2+28x-20$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Integer zeroes: $-1,2$.\n$P(x)=(2x-5)(3x-2)(x+1)(x-2)$; the remaining zeroes are $\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{2}{3}$.",
          "worked": "Possible integer zeroes are factors of $20$. Begin with $\\pm1,\\pm2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=6-25+17+28-20=6\\\\P(-1)&=6+25+17-28-20=0\\\\P(2)&=96-200+68+56-20=0\\\\P(-2)&=96+200+68-56-20=288.\\end{align*}$$\nLong division by $x+1$ gives quotient $6x^3-31x^2+48x-20$ and remainder $0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)-6x^3(x+1)&=-31x^3+17x^2+28x-20\\\\{}-(-31x^2)(x+1)&=48x^2+28x-20\\\\{}-48x(x+1)&=-20x-20\\\\{}-(-20)(x+1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nDivide the quotient by $x-2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(6x^3-31x^2+48x-20)-6x^2(x-2)&=-19x^2+48x-20\\\\{}-(-19x)(x-2)&=10x-20\\\\{}-10(x-2)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(x-2)(6x^2-19x+10)\\\\&=(x+1)(x-2)(2x-5)(3x-2).\\end{align*}$$\nThe zeroes are $-1,2,\\frac52,\\frac23$, so the only integer zeroes are $-1$ and $2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 130
      }
    ]
  },
